<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fucine Lake</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Lake Fucinus, Lago Fucino</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Fucine Lake was a large lake in the central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apennines">Apennines</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abruzzo">Abruzzo</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, around which the Marsi lived. Its uncontrolled floods prompted the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/claudius">Claudius</a> to cut a drainage tunnel in the 1st century CE, though the lake was fully drained only in the 19th century under Prince Alessandro Torlonia. Its former bed is now a fertile plain.</p></div>
